 the works received at most 12% of the citations expected for similar works worldwide (FWCI 1 = world average).","Above the world average: 0%–7% of the works per year have an FWCI above 1, most in 2019 (7%).","Not cited: on average 65% of these works have FWCI 0, meaning no citations within their four-year window. That is why many boxes start at 0.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 10 of 13 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2021: mean 0.23, median 0.12, top work 1.31. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Still counting: works from 2023–2026 have not completed their four-year citation window, so their values will rise. Do not compare them with older years yet.","Small base: the values for 2009–2015 and 2017–2026 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2016 has fewer than 10 works (2016: 7), too few for a box. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2009–2023 have a median of 0–2 citations each; the highest median (2) is in 6 of 14 years.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2012 have at least 11 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2024–2026 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 13 of 14 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2010: mean 3.1, median 1, top work 26. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Recent years: works from 2024–2026 have had less than three years to be cited, so their values will rise.","Small base: the values for 2009–2015 and 2017–2026 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2016 has fewer than 10 works (2016: 7), too few for a band. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."]}}}